pb1_spec.dat is an unchanged copy of vtcalcs/data/specdata/pb1_spec.dat.
../maeda.py is a modified, differentiable PyTorch port of the geometry math in
vtcalcs/src/lam_lib.c. Vowel presets are from vtcalcs/src/Vtcalcs.c (vowelpar)
and the matching vtcalcs/arcb.m table (Copyright (c) 1999 Satrajit S. Ghosh).
The original implementation is by Shinji Maeda, adapted to MATLAB by Satrajit Ghosh.

Changes: batched tensors; sigmoid-bounded parameters; independent velum;
cm coordinates mirrored to face +x, glottal midpoint origin; speaker scaling;
cross-product quadrilateral areas; equal-midline-length area integration and
contour interpolation; numerical floors. No original acoustic simulator or
Track Draw code is included. The original 1.10 size correction and documented
1.4 ad-hoc sagittal-to-area correction are retained.

The seven-factor model is described in:
Shinji Maeda (1990), Compensatory Articulation During Speech: Evidence from the
Analysis and Synthesis of Vocal-Tract Shapes Using an Articulatory Model,
Speech Production and Speech Modelling, pp. 131–149.
https://doi.org/10.1007/978-94-009-2037-8_6
The presets here are source-code examples, not verified values from that paper.

